title: stop() leaves the queue populated, stalling a key after restart
updated: 2026-08-13T01:50:43Z
---

Found while working on 10 and 11, read from the code and not reproduced by a test. stop() clears the retry futures but leaves the queue array filled and the queued flags set on the entries. After a stop/start cycle an event for an already-queued key returns early without scheduling a drain, so that key sits idle until some unrelated key arrives and drains the queue behind it. Pre-existing and independent of both tickets. Decide whether stop() clears the queue and the flags, or start() reschedules a drain when the queue is non-empty. Needs a test covering the stop/start cycle.
